.TH GENESYS-GUI 1 "2026-08-20" "GenESyS" "GenESyS Manual"
.SH NAME
genesys-gui \- GenESyS Qt graphical simulation environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genesys-gui
.RI [ --check-only | --no-update ]
.RI [ --help | --version ]
.RB [ -- ]
.RI [ application-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesys-gui
is the stable public entry point for the GenESyS graphical user interface. It
is a small wrapper that execs
.BR /usr/libexec/genesys/genesys-launcher (8)
with
.B --app genesys-gui
and
.BR --interactive-update .
The launcher selects either the validated per-user runtime referenced by
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
or the Debian-provided system fallback installed at
.I /usr/libexec/genesys/system/bin/genesys-gui
and then replaces itself with the selected GUI executable.
.PP
.B genesys-gui
is the only GenESyS public command that is allowed to perform an interactive,
network-based update check. The Shell, Worker, legacy Web and MCP entry
points never contact the network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check-only
Check whether an update is available and exit without prompting or starting
the GUI.
.TP
.B --no-update
Never perform a network update check, overriding the wrapper's default
interactive check request and the administrative
.I check_on_gui_startup
setting.
.TP
.B --help ", " -h
Print launcher usage information and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Print the launcher version and exit.
.TP
.RI [ application-arguments "...]"
Any remaining arguments are forwarded unchanged to the selected GUI
executable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/genesys/update.conf
System-wide administrative update policy (conffile). Values here take
precedence over the per-user configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/genesys/update.conf
Optional per-user update configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
Symbolic link selecting the active per-user runtime, if any.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/genesys/launcher.log
Launcher activity log.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the selected GUI executable, or 127 if no valid runtime
could be selected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesys-shell (1),
.BR genesys-worker (1),
.BR genesys-mcp (1)
